Sure! Here is an interface with generics:
```ts
interface Box<T> {
  value: T;
}
const box: Box<string> = { value: 'hello' };
```
This works for any type T.

You can constrain generics with extends:
```ts
function getLength<T extends { length: number }>(arg: T): number {
  return arg.length;
}
```
